ggans consolidates incumbents' typical Election-Day advantage.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 86 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Jen Kiggans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 2nd District is a rematch between incumbent Republican Jen Kiggans and Democrat Elaine Luria, who held the seat before losing it in 2022. The district is politically even, and the race is among the most-watched House contests nationally. Kiggans has a modest fundraising edge, but Luria has kept pace with strong cash on hand.\n\nExpert ratings tilt Democratic, with several outlets calling the seat a likely or lean Democratic flip and two calling it a tossup. Prediction markets give Luria roughly an 80% chance, and reports of early voting shifting toward Democrats reinforce that lean. The only public poll, from July, showed a dead heat, so hard polling evidence remains thin and the race could tighten.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.777, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7659, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.762, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7557, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7851, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7923, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8055, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8023, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8046, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8169, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7631, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7572, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 5.0}]}